# Customer Proof Rule

Apply this selector-first rule to connector-bound blog drafts, rewrites, and the production BOM's proof items.

## Connector-bound Simpro workflows

Before selecting customer proof, resolve `topic`, `title`, and `objective`, then run:

```powershell
python data_sources/modules/customer_proof_selector.py "[topic]" --title "[title]" --objective "[objective]" --context-pack "research/context-pack-[slug].json" --context-receipt "research/context-receipt-[slug].json" --evidence-output "research/customer-proof-selector-evidence-[slug].json" --slate --roles metric,quote,theme,experience_story --require-eeat-story --limit 10
```

Add `--decision-block` to print a prefilled `Customer Proof Selection Decision` whose `Selected proof` lines match the slate. It is a private research note: keep it with the research brief, and append `Reuse reason`, the zero-use comparison, and `Final use in copy` directly under its bullets with no blank line.

For review-derived public E-E-A-T stories, also run:

```powershell
python data_sources/modules/customer_proof_selector.py "[topic]" --title "[title]" --objective "[objective]" --context-pack "research/context-pack-[slug].json" --context-receipt "research/context-receipt-[slug].json" --evidence-output "research/customer-proof-selector-evidence-[slug].json" --slate --roles experience_story --require-eeat-story --limit 10
```

Simpro candidates come exclusively from approved claim results bound to the current context pack and receipt. The selector requires complete, non-truncated task-specific claim searches for `public_metric`, `exact_quote`, and `public_paraphrase`, uses `claim_id` as the candidate identifier, and fails closed on legacy local `--index` use.

The selector evidence file is the record of the slate. The production BOM build binds it by path and sha256 and admits a proof item only when its `claim_id` is an approved claim in the validated context receipt and a selected candidate in that evidence. The release refreshes the evidence so it is same-day before rebuilding the BOM. If inputs are missing or the selector fails, record the blocker in the research brief and do not invent proof.

## Selection and reuse

Choose the most relevant approved claim, not the easiest searchable case study. Treat any `recent_uses_90d` value above 0 as a proof-diversity warning. Prefer an approved zero-recent-use source when one fits the same role. Before claiming a proof source is underused, inspect `config/customer-proof-usage-ledger.json` and run a live repo scan across `drafts/`, `rewrites/`, `research/`, and `published/` for the claim ID, public URL, and customer name. If public-copy usage is missing from the ledger, backfill `config/customer-proof-usage-ledger.json`, rerun selector checks, and document the backfill in the research brief.

When selected proof is recently used or overused, add a `Customer Proof Selection Decision` and source-specific `Reuse reason` proving no stronger underused approved claim fits the same role.

## Nonconnector workflows

AroFlo, BigChange, and ClockShark owned workflows with no Simpro name or official `simprogroup.com` URL are nonconnector. Do not run the vault-dependent selector. When the separate non-vault proof contract applies, run the nonvault selector against `config/nonvault-customer-proof-index.json` and require `simpro-nonvault-customer-proof-selector-evidence/v1`.

Run `python data_sources/modules/nonvault_customer_proof_selector.py "[topic]" --brand "[brand]" --title "[title]" --objective "[objective]" --article-slug "[slug]" --index config/nonvault-customer-proof-index.json --ledger config/customer-proof-usage-ledger.json --evidence-output "research/nonvault-customer-proof-selector-evidence-[slug].json" --slate --roles metric,quote,theme,experience_story --require-eeat-story --limit 10` for eligible nonconnector proof workflows. V1 permits approved brand-owned customer stories, case studies, and references, plus approved Capterra `review_site` rows on the brand's listed product page. Review-derived stories are paraphrased with a same-paragraph review link; exact snippets are allowed only when stored in that row's `approved_quotes` and live-captured. It does not permit ratings, stars, aggregate ratings, rankings, review metrics, or named-person attribution beyond the approved review row; avoid the words "reviewer", "rated", and "stars" in public copy.

Run `python data_sources/modules/customer_proof_index_health.py --index config/nonvault-customer-proof-index.json --ledger config/customer-proof-usage-ledger.json` only for nonconnector inventory health. Add new nonconnector proof candidates through an intake CSV and validate them with `python data_sources/modules/customer_proof_index_intake.py validate [input.csv] --index config/nonvault-customer-proof-index.json`.

## Public-copy use

Selected customer proof reaches public copy only as a production BOM proof item. The release renders the `Selected Customer Proof Mining` view from the BOM for the scorer, and blocks a customer or review claim that links no BOM proof URL. Its quote check matches every quoted passage against all BOM text, approved proof quotes and fact quotes alike, and requires it to sit verbatim in one source: it blocks a blockquote that is not a labeled callout, and an attributed inline quote of `MIN_ATTRIBUTED_WORDS` (2) or more words; an unattributed inline quote of 4 or more words only warns. When selected customer proof appears in public copy, add a matching entry to `config/customer-proof-usage-ledger.json` before final handoff; the release never writes the ledger. Review-derived E-E-A-T stories require same-paragraph public review links. Use `context/aeo-geo-blog-strategy.md` as the canonical policy.
